    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/214438": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Open Rank Faculty Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Open Rank Faculty Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email . Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number FAC00102PO26 Advertised Title Open Rank Faculty Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management Campus Beaufort College/Division USC Beaufort College/Division Level Department BFT Hospitality Management Advertised Salary Range Salary commensurate with qualifications Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Position Category Full-time Equivalent (FTE) Basis 9 months Work County Beaufort Tenure Information Tenure-Track/Tenured Job Search Category Faculty About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers state employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The University of South Carolina Beaufort ( USCB ) invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track, open-rank faculty position in the Department of Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management, beginning August 16, 2027. The rank of Assistant or Associate Professor will be determined based on the qualifications and experience of the selected candidate. The Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management program offers a Bachelor of Science degree with campus-based and online opportunities. The program prepares students for professional careers in the hospitality and tourism industries, including lodging, food and beverage, resort and club management, tourism, and event management. Located in the Lowcountry of South Carolina, USCB provides faculty and students with exceptional opportunities to engage with regional hospitality and tourism organizations and to incorporate experiential learning into the curriculum. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching, scholarship, student engagement, and service. Teaching responsibilities will include undergraduate courses in Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management and related areas, with opportunities to teach courses in areas such as event management, human resources, leadership, and hospitality management. Courses may be delivered in face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online formats on the Bluffton and Hilton Head Island campuses and through USCB’s online programs. The standard teaching load is 4/4. Teaching: Teach undergraduate courses in Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management and related disciplines; develop and deliver engaging, student-centered instruction across face-to-face, hybrid, and online modalities; advise and mentor students; and contribute to curriculum development and assessment. The successful candidate will support experiential and applied learning opportunities that connect classroom instruction with the hospitality and tourism industry. Scholarship: Maintain an active program of scholarship appropriate to the candidate’s area of expertise and rank. Scholarly activities may include peer-reviewed publications, professional presentations, applied research, grants, and other contributions to the discipline. Candidates are expected to engage undergraduate students in research, applied projects, and other scholarly or professional activities as appropriate. Contributions to the scholarship of teaching and learning are encouraged. Service: Participate in shared governance and provide service to the program, department, college, and university through committee participation, student advising and mentoring, program assessment, recruitment, and other assigned responsibilities. The successful candidate will also contribute to professional and community service and develop relationships with hospitality and tourism industry partners. Collaboration with the faculty to strengthen connections between USCB and the regional hospitality and tourism community connections with local leaders and foster meaningful experiential learning opportunities for hospitality students. This 9-month tenure-track position begins on August 16, 2027, and is being advertised as an open-rank position depending on qualifications. Salary is commensurate with experience. Required Education and Experience Doctoral degree in Hospitality Management, Tourism, or related field from an accredited institution. Ph.D. preferred but will consider other terminal degrees. ABDs will be considered as long as the degree is earned by the start date. Preferred Qualifications Previous work and/or teaching experience in the field of Hospitality or Tourism. Certified Hospitality Educator (CHE®) credentialing is a plus. Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email . Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212887 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a terminal degree in Hospitality Management, Tourism, or related field from an accredited institution? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Other Supporting Documents Research Portfolio Resume Teaching Portfolio Research Statement To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
